# Keeping Pages Fresh

After a mutation (create, update, delete), you want the UI to reflect the change.

Server Actions can call `revalidatePath()` or `revalidateTag()` to purge the cache and refetch data.

```js
import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache';

export async function addPost(formData) {
  await db.post.create(...);
  revalidatePath('/posts');
}
```

Now the `/posts` page will show the new post immediately.

slides.codeSnippet:
// app/actions.js
'use server';
import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache';

export async function createProduct(formData) {
  const name = formData.get('name');
  // db.product.create({ name });
  revalidatePath('/products');
}

